High Points (Strengths)

Premium Models: iPhone 15 Pro Max, iPhone 16 Pro, and iPhone Air drive high‑ticket sales, especially among 25–45 age group.
Finance EMI Popularity: EMI widely adopted across age groups, showing strong demand for flexible payments.
Branch Leaders: Ruby and Mukundopur consistently generate maximum revenue.
Color Preferences: Blue, Red, and White dominate customer demand.
Storage Demand: 512GB and 1TB models preferred by professionals and younger buyers.

Low Points (Weaknesses)

Older Models: iPhone 12 and SE sell at lower price points, often via cash, reducing revenue contribution.
Weak Branches: Kasba and Behala lag behind Ruby/Mukundopur.
Age Group Gaps: Customers above 50 buy less frequently and prefer cheaper models.
Payment Imbalance: UPI and Debit Card usage lower compared to EMI and Credit Card.
Locality Weak Spots: Picnic Garden and Topsia show weaker revenue compared to Gariahat and Tollygunge.

Conversion Strategies (Low → High)

Upgrade Campaigns: Trade‑in offers for SE/12 buyers → upgrade to iPhone 15/16; bundle accessories to increase ticket size.
Branch Revitalization: Localized promotions in Kasba/Behala; cross‑branch mentoring by Ruby/Mukundopur sales leaders.
Age Group Engagement: Highlight ease‑of‑use features for 50+ customers; introduce senior‑friendly EMI plans.
Payment Expansion: Incentivize UPI/Debit with cashback; partner with banks for co‑branded EMI cards.
Locality Marketing: Targeted ads in Picnic Garden/Topsia; free delivery and exclusive in‑store experiences.

📊 Research Recommendations

Customer Segmentation: Analyze age + payment behavior for tailored offers.
Branch Benchmarking: Compare Ruby/Mukundopur vs Kasba/Behala to identify operational gaps.
Seasonality Analysis: Study monthly sales trends to align promotions with peak buying periods.
Color & Storage Forecasting: Stock more Blue/Red models with 512GB+ storage to meet demand spikes.
Salesperson Performance: Evaluate revenue contribution by individual salespersons; reward top performers and train weaker ones.
Payment Method Optimization: Assess EMI vs Cash vs UPI adoption; design campaigns to balance usage and improve conversion flexibility.
Age Group Trend Analysis: Compare buying behavior across age brackets; design senior‑friendly offers for 50+ customers.
Profitability Analysis: Calculate margin contribution by model, branch, and payment method to prioritize high‑profit segments.
Cross‑Selling Opportunities: Recommend accessories (AirPods, AppleCare, cases) bundled with premium models to increase ticket size.
Customer Retention Analysis: Track repeat buyers and design loyalty programs to maximize lifetime value.










